        {
          "type": "code",
          "say": "So zero-one knapsack runs the capacity loop from W down to the item's weight. The one-dimensional array is the two-dimensional table, with the rows overwritten in place, and the backward loop keeps each read on the old row. Subset sum, equal partition, and target sum are the same loop, storing a bool or a count instead of a value. O of n times W time, O of W space.",
          "props": {
            "title": "Backward = <em>once</em>",
            "file": "knapsack01.cpp",
            "tag": "C++",
            "lang": "cpp",
            "size": 21,
            "width": 1250,
            "code": "int knapsack01(int W, const vector<int>& wt, const vector<int>& val) {\n    vector<int> dp(W + 1, 0);               // dp[w]: best value within capacity w\n    for (int i = 0; i < (int)wt.size(); ++i)\n        for (int w = W; w >= wt[i]; --w)    // backward: dp[w - wt[i]] is still old\n            dp[w] = max(dp[w], dp[w - wt[i]] + val[i]);\n    return dp[W];\n}",
            "highlights": [
              {
                "at": "down",
                "lines": "4",
                "note": "Capacity loop runs backward"
              },
              {
                "at": "overwritten",
                "lines": "2",
                "note": "One row, overwritten in place"
              },
              {
                "at": "old",
                "lines": "5",
                "note": "dp[w − wt] is still the old row"
              },
              {
                "at": "bool",
                "lines": "3-5",
                "note": "Subset sum: bool; target sum: count"
              }
            ]
          }
        }
