        },
        {
          "type": "compare",
          "say": "Coins one and two, amount three. Put the coins in the outer loop, and every way is built in coin order: all the ones, then all the twos. So one plus two is counted once: two ways in total, one-one-one, and one-two. Put the amount in the outer loop, and each step tries every coin as the last one. Now one plus two and two plus one are different sequences: three ways. Combinations: coins outside. Permutations: amount outside.",
